| §C8 — wheel-coprime cumulative Liouville identity (S219, paradigm-shift mode): is `L_W(x) := Σ_{n ≤ x, gcd(n, W) = 1} λ(n)` reducible to a finite signed sum of unrestricted Liouville sums `L(⌊x/d⌋)` indexed by divisors of `rad(W)`, and does the wheel-graded bisection π_W(x) = (1/2)(n_W(x) − L_W(x)) − C_{3,W}(x) admit a closed-form divisor-sum decomposition? | REFINEMENT | E (refinement of E1.6 / E2.10) | S219 paradigm-shift session — no cross-domain imports. Composes E1.6 (cumulative bisection π = (x − L)/2 − C_3) with E2.10 (L mod 2 = x mod 2) and E2.1/E4.1/S208 (wheel-W density `φ(W)/W`, indicator-side `T_W^{div}`). **Theorem 1** (proven analytically + integer-exact verified at 16 W × ~200 x cells with N = 10⁴): `L_W(x) = Σ_{d | rad(W)} L(⌊x/d⌋)` for every W ≥ 1 and integer x ≥ 0. RHS has exactly `2^{ω(W)}` terms, depends on W only through `rad(W)`. Proof: Möbius expand `[gcd(n,W)=1]`, swap summation order, use `λ(dm) = λ(d)λ(m)` (completely multiplicative), collapse `μ(d)λ(d) = +1` for squarefree `d` and `0` otherwise. **Theorem 2** (proven + verified): `L_W(x) mod 2 = (Σ_{d | rad(W)} ⌊x/d⌋) mod 2`. Computable in `O(ω(W))` ops without any L-oracle. **Theorem 3** (wheel-graded bisection lift): `π_W(x) = (1/2) Σ_{d | rad(W)} (μ(d)⌊x/d⌋ − L(⌊x/d⌋)) − C_{3,W}(x)`, integer-exact verified at 16 W × 4 x cells. **F1-F6 all PASS** integer-exact. **Algorithmic content**: `2^{ω(W)}`-call oracle reduction `L_W → L`, polylog in W for primorial W (since `2^{ω(W)} = W^{O(1/log log W)}`); does NOT bypass the unconditional `O(x^{2/3})` ceiling for `L(x)` (the oracle bottleneck). **Why B not A**: classical Möbius inversion + completely-multiplicative `λ`, derivable in an afternoon by an analytic NT theorist. **Why B not C**: clean integer-exact pointwise identity + wheel-graded bisection lift + `2^{ω(W)}` reduction, none previously stated in EDGES.md / `experiments/` / sessions; symmetric counterpart to S208's pointwise indicator-side `T_W^{div}`. Refines E1.6 and E2.10 inline. Successor challenges added (NOVELTY_CHALLENGES.md §C8, §C8.b). **Cross-domain ingredient**: NONE imported (paradigm-shift mode). Tools used: Möbius inversion + completely-multiplicative property of `λ`, both already-`USED` in CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md from prior sessions. See `experiments/constructions/wheel_coprime_liouville_identity/{definition.md, wheel_coprime_liouville.py, wheel_coprime_liouville_results.md, wheel_coprime_liouville_results.json, run.log}`, `archive/sessions/session219_paradigm_shift_wheel_liouville.md`. | 219 |
